<title>SWITZERLAND: Tag Heuer shares open at 260 Sfr.</title>
<headline>Tag Heuer shares open at 260 Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>New bearer shares of Swiss watchmaker TAG Heuer SA started trading at 260 Swiss francs ($207.9) on the Swiss Exchange, 15 francs higher than the shares were sold at during the Initial Public Offering (IPO).</p>
<p>At 0810 GMT, 10 minutes after trading started, the shares had eased to 255 francs.</p>
<p>A total of 12,630 shares had been traded for a turnover of 3.2 million francs.</p>
<p>TAG Heuer's share offering was heavily oversubscribed, both in the United States and international tranches, which each took half the shares of offer.</p>
<p>Earlier this week TAG Heuer raised the size of the public offering by around 35 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340 ($1=1.2505 Swiss Franc)</p>
